cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MRRpy, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "MRRpy: A modular Python model for distributed rainfall–runoff generation and flood routing"
abstract: >-
  MRRpy (Multi-Mechanism Runoff and Routing) is an open-source Python package
  for distributed, event-scale rainfall–runoff simulation and channel flood
  routing. From a DEM it delineates a D8 drainage network, generates runoff by
  interchangeable methods (runoff coefficient, SCS Curve Number, or a
  process-based combination of variable-source-area saturation-excess,
  Green–Ampt infiltration-excess and impervious runoff), and routes it with
  kinematic-wave, Muskingum–Cunge or semi-implicit diffusive-wave schemes,
  driven by one configuration through a Python API, CLI, Jupyter form or QGIS
  plugin, with optional Google Earth Engine forcing and GPU acceleration.
